<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Mouse Operations</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>KUBE uses actively the mouse for different operations on the viewport. Most of mouse actions concern rotating and translating the viewport. While holding the left mouse button on the viewable area, user can perform rotate, pan, or zoom depending on the current mode.</p>
<p><img src="../images/hand_and_mouse.gif" width="240px" height="171px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>There are four modes for changing viewpoint by the mouse. You can switch between them from the toolbar or the viewport context menu.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span class="Mode">Zoom Window</span>  default mode.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + Left mouse button</span> or only <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Right mouse button</b></span> will temporary switch to <span class="Mode">Rotate</span> mode.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + Middle mouse button</span> or only the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>mouse wheel</b></span> will temporary switch to <span class="Mode">Zoom</span> mode.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Using <span class="Shortcut">Shift + Right mouse button</span> or only <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Middle mouse button</b></span> will temporary switch to <span class="Mode">Pan</span> mode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: When you release the <span class="Shortcut">Shift</span> button, KUBE will switch to the previous mode.</p>
<p>Double click on the viewport will switch between <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Mode">Points</span></u> rendering mode and the current rendering mode. For example, if the current mode is <span class="Mode">Flat</span> and you double click, the scene will be displayed in <span class="Mode">Points</span> mode. When you double click again, you will return to <span class="Mode">Flat</span> mode.</p>
<p>When in <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Rotate</u></span> or <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Pan</u></span> mode manipulations with the mouse are infinite. This means that if the mouse cursor exit from the screen it automatically appears at the opposite side of the screen if the mouse continue in the same direction.</p>
